\section{What the heuristics change}
\label{sec:heuristics}

Each design choice of a JEPA enters the race of \cref{sec:race} through a definite term: the data quantities $(c_k,\sigma_k)$, the starting point $(p_0,a_0)$, or the clock $1/(\alpha\lambda_P)$ on which the predictor gain decays.
At initialisation these are the doses of \citet{demelocosta2026drive} (predictor scale, an encoder-decay floor, EMA speed, mask retention; \cref{app:related}); the race adds the clock, which decides survival from above the window and $\lambda^{\mathrm{race}}$.
\Cref{tab:heuristics} maps each choice to the term it moves and to a prediction with a sign; \cref{sec:experiments} reports the tests.
We write $F_k^*$ for the value of \eqref{eq:F} at $p=p_-^k$, so that $\partial F_k^*/\partial p_0=g_k(p_0)/(\alpha\lambda_Pp_0)$.
